  "_riders_note": "Rider composites, keyed archetype -> class. Extracted against their OWN archetype (extract_riders.py <cls> <composite> <base>), which is what makes leftover fragments invisible: stray pixels are that mount's pixels going back onto that mount. The eight plain quadrupeds share the horse-extracted layer; only visually distinct mounts need their own.",
  "_rider_plan": "ONE rider silhouette (knight) for all 17 classes; class identity is deferred to the SKIN system, not baked. Only visually distinct mounts need their own extraction -- the seven plain quadrupeds (destrier, mule, stag, elk, boar, ram, cat) share the horse layer, because extraction fragments only show when a layer moves to a differently-coloured animal."
